          "jcr:created": "Wed Sep 11 2019 19:43:16 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p><b>Description:&nbsp;</b>Dr. Adams and Dr. Palanca discuss their experiences with total ankle replacements covering everything from patient selection to post-operative protocol. Hear their similarities and differences in opinions on various approaches in this total ankle replacement course.</p>\n<p><b>Learning objective:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cover patient selection factors such as age, arthritis stage, smoking factors, activity level</li>\n<li>Best practices for wound management</li>\n<li>Discuss the mobile bearing total ankle</li>\n<li>Understanding different types of ankle deformity as it relates to total ankle replacement</li>\n<li>Describing ancillary procedures that can be done concurrently or staged with ankle replacement</li>\n<li>Defining post-operative protocols for ankle replacement</li>\n<li>Discuss tips &amp; tricks related to the STAR prosthesis</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Course instructor: <br>\n</b>Samuel Adams, MD and&nbsp;Ariel Palanca, MD</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Oct 30 2019 18:37:52 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
